This Synesis Data-Output Exception ("this Exception") is an additional
permission under section 7 of the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3 ("AGPLv3"). It applies to a given file (the "Covered Code")
that bears a notice placed by the copyright holder stating that the file
is governed by the AGPLv3 with this Exception.

This Exception is modeled on the GCC Runtime Library Exception and the
Bison parser exception, which establish that the output of a program is
not, by that fact alone, a derivative work of the program that produced
it.


0. Definitions.

"Synesis" means the compiler, language server, code-generation tools, and
associated libraries distributed by the copyright holder under the AGPLv3
together with this Exception — including, without limitation, the packages
`synesis`, `synesis-lsp`, `synesis-coder`, and `synesis-graph`.

"Input" means any file authored or supplied by a user and given to Synesis
for processing, including but not limited to files with the extensions
`.syn`, `.synt`, `.synp`, and `.syno`, as well as bibliographic sources
(such as BibTeX `.bib` files) and any other user-supplied data.

"Output" means any material produced by running Synesis on Input,
including but not limited to: canonical JSON, CSV tables, Excel workbooks
(`.xlsx`), Alpaca JSONL datasets, knowledge-graph exports (such as Neo4j
or Cypher artifacts and HTML visualizations), diagnostics, and any other
compiled, transformed, or exported artifact derived from the Input.

"Synesis Runtime Material" means portions of Synesis's own source code
that Synesis embeds automatically into an Output for the sole purpose of
enabling that Output to be displayed, formatted, executed, or otherwise
function as intended — for example, the JavaScript, CSS, HTML scaffolding,
and template code emitted into a generated knowledge-graph visualization,
or fixed instruction/scaffolding text emitted into a generated dataset.
Synesis Runtime Material is embedded by Synesis on the user's behalf as an
ordinary consequence of generating the Output; it is distinct from source
code of Synesis that a user deliberately copies out of Synesis and into a
separate work.

For the avoidance of doubt, "Output" does not include source code of
Synesis that a user deliberately copies, verbatim or modified, out of
Synesis into a distributed work — other than Synesis Runtime Material
embedded automatically as described above.


1. Grant of Exception.

You have permission to use, propagate, and convey the Output produced by
running Synesis on your Input under terms of your choice, without those
terms being subject to the AGPLv3 by reason of the Output having been
produced by Synesis.

This permission extends to any Synesis Runtime Material that Synesis
embeds automatically into the Output. You may convey such Output, together
with the Synesis Runtime Material it contains, under terms of your choice,
and you are not required to license that Output under the AGPLv3 by reason
of the embedded Synesis Runtime Material. This mirrors the GCC Runtime
Library Exception: just as a program compiled with GCC may carry GCC
runtime code and still be licensed freely, an Output generated by Synesis
may carry Synesis Runtime Material and still be licensed freely.

The AGPLv3 and this Exception impose no restriction on, and assert no
copyright interest in, the Output. As between you and the copyright
holder of Synesis, you retain all rights you hold in your Input and in
the Output generated from it. The Output is not, by reason of having been
produced by Synesis (including by reason of embedded Synesis Runtime
Material), a work "based on" Synesis within the meaning of the AGPLv3.


2. Scope and Limits of the Exception.

This Exception concerns only the Output as defined above. It does NOT
grant any additional permission with respect to Synesis itself.

In particular, this Exception does not permit you to:

  (a) remove or alter the AGPLv3 obligations that apply when you copy,
      modify, distribute, or make available over a network (including as
      a service) the source code of Synesis or any work based on it; or

  (b) deliberately copy Synesis's own source code out of Synesis into your
      Output or into any other work, and then rely on this Exception to
      avoid the AGPLv3. If you copy a portion of Synesis's source code by
      hand into a work (as opposed to material generated from your Input,
      or Synesis Runtime Material embedded automatically by Synesis under
      section 1), that copied portion remains governed by the AGPLv3.

      Synesis Runtime Material that Synesis embeds automatically into an
      Output is covered by the grant in section 1 and does NOT fall under
      this restriction.

Nothing in this Exception limits the permissions you already have under
the AGPLv3.


3. No Warranty.

This Exception does not alter the disclaimer of warranty or limitation of
liability set out in the AGPLv3, which continue to apply in full.


